      "content": "idk, it's hard to say \"both sides\" were equally at fault when looking at the scale of what happened. like, if you look at the actual expulsion of people and the loss of land, isn't it more accurate to say the primary driver was a deliberate policy of displacement by the new state, rather than just \"military actions on both sides\"? feels like calling it a \"conflict\" minimizes the fact that one side fundamentally lost everything.",
