      "content": "It is accurate to recognize that the impact of the conflict on the Palestinian population involved massive displacement and loss of land, leading many scholars to analyze it through the lens of dispossession. While military conflict was part of the dynamic, many historical analyses point to institutional policies and decisions made by the emerging Israeli state as a significant catalyst for the outcome. Framing the period requires acknowledging the differing experiences: one narrative centers on state-building, while the other emphasizes the systematic displacement of an existing population. Balancing these realities is key to avoiding simplistic attribution of sole blame.",
